## 2. Code Language Standards

### 2.1 English-Only Code Rule

**CRITICAL: All source code files (excluding `docs/` directory) MUST use English.**

#### Must Use English
- ✅ Code comments (single-line, multi-line, JSDoc)
- ✅ Variable and function names
- ✅ Error messages
- ✅ Console output
- ✅ String literals (internal)
- ✅ Type definitions

#### Allowed Chinese
- ✅ `docs/` directory files
- ✅ `README.md`
- ✅ `env.example` comments

#### Forbidden Chinese
- ❌ All source files (`app/`, `components/`, `lib/`, `types/`)
- ❌ Code comments
- ❌ Variable/function names
- ❌ Error messages
- ❌ Console output

---

## 3. Brand Information Standards

### 3.1 Brand Configuration

**CRITICAL: Always use centralized brand configuration.**

#### Configuration File
- **File**: `lib/metadata.ts`
- **Variable**: `siteConfig`

#### Brand Information
```typescript
export const siteConfig = {
  name: 'MaxTool',
  shortName: 'MaxTool',
  domain: 'maxtool.me',
  url: 'https://maxtool.me',
  description: 'Free online tools for everyday tasks. Simple, fast, and no registration required.',
  slogan: 'Free Online Tools - Simple & Fast',
}
```

#### Rules
- ✅ ALWAYS import from `lib/metadata.ts`
- ✅ NEVER hardcode brand information
- ✅ Use `siteConfig.name` instead of "MaxTool" string
- ✅ Use `siteConfig.url` instead of hardcoded URLs

---

## 4. SEO Standards

### 4.1 Metadata Generation

**CRITICAL: Use centralized metadata generation functions.**

#### Functions Location
- **File**: `lib/metadata.ts`

#### Usage Rules
- ✅ Homepage: Use `generateBaseMetadata()`
- ✅ Tool pages: Use `generateToolMetadata(toolName, toolDescription, toolPath)`
- ✅ Category pages: Use `generateCategoryMetadata(categoryName, categoryPath, toolCount)`

#### Structured Data
- **File**: `lib/structured-data.ts`
- **Component**: `components/shared/StructuredData.tsx`
- **Rule**: All pages MUST include appropriate structured data

### 4.2 URL Path SEO Optimization

**CRITICAL: Tool URLs MUST use two-level category structure for SEO.**

#### URL Structure Requirements
- ✅ **Format**: `/tools/[category]/[tool-id]`
- ✅ **Categories**: `random`, `time`, `text`, `utilities`, `other`
- ✅ **SEO Benefit**: Category keywords in URL improve search rankings
- ✅ **Category Pages**: `/tools/[category]` provides category-level SEO

#### Sitemap Configuration
- **File**: `app/sitemap.ts`
- **Rule**: Include both tool pages and category pages
- **Priority**:
  - Tool pages: `priority: 1.0`
  - Category pages: `priority: 0.9`
  - Legacy category pages: `priority: 0.8`

#### Breadcrumb Navigation
- **File**: `components/shared/Breadcrumb.tsx`
- **Rule**: Support `/tools/[category]/[tool-id]` path format
- **Pattern**: `Home > [Category] Tools > [Tool Name]`

---

## 5. Theme & Styling Standards

### 5.1 Theme Variables

**CRITICAL: Use theme variables, NEVER hardcode colors.**

#### Theme Variables Location
- **File**: `app/globals.css`
- **Pattern**: Use CSS variables defined in `@theme` and `@layer theme .dark`

#### Color Usage Rules
- ✅ Use semantic color variables: `bg-accent`, `text-accent`, `bg-error`, `text-error`
- ✅ Use theme-aware colors: `bg-bg-primary`, `text-text-primary`, `border-border`
- ❌ NEVER use hardcoded colors: `bg-blue-500`, `text-red-600`, `dark:bg-gray-900`

#### Semantic Colors Available
- `accent`, `accent-hover`, `accent-light`
- `success`, `success-bg`, `success-text`, `success-border`
- `error`, `error-bg`, `error-text`, `error-border`
- `warning`, `warning-bg`, `warning-text`, `warning-border`
- `info`, `info-bg`, `info-text`, `info-border`

#### Dark Mode Support
- ✅ ALL components MUST support dark mode
- ✅ Use theme variables that automatically adapt
- ✅ Test in both light and dark modes

---

## 6. URL & Routing Standards

### 6.1 URL Path Structure (CRITICAL)

**CRITICAL: All tool URLs MUST use two-level category structure for SEO optimization.**

#### Tool URL Format
- **Format**: `/tools/[category]/[tool-id]`
- **Example**: `/tools/random/random-number`, `/tools/time/countdown-timer`
- **Categories**: `random`, `time`, `text`, `utilities`, `other`

#### Rules
- ✅ **MUST use two-level path**: `/tools/[category]/[tool-id]`
- ✅ Use lowercase: `/tools/random/random-number` (correct)
- ✅ Use kebab-case: `/tools/random/random-number` (correct)
- ✅ Use hyphens: `/tools/random/random-number` (correct)
- ❌ **NEVER use flat path**: `/tools/random-number` (wrong - only for legacy)
- ❌ No uppercase: `/tools/Random/RandomNumber` (wrong)
- ❌ No underscores: `/tools/random/random_number` (wrong)
- ❌ No spaces: `/tools/random/random number` (wrong)

#### SEO Benefits
- ✅ Category keywords in URL (`random`, `time`, `text`, `utilities`)
- ✅ Supports category aggregation pages (`/tools/[category]`)
- ✅ Better internal linking structure
- ✅ Clearer hierarchy for search engines

#### Path Generation
- **File**: `lib/tools-data.ts`
- **Rule**: All tool `path` fields MUST follow `/tools/[category]/[tool-id]` format
- **Example**:
  ```typescript
  {
    id: 'random-number',
    category: 'Random',
    path: '/tools/random/random-number',  // ✅ Correct
    // path: '/tools/random-number',      // ❌ Wrong
  }
  ```

### 6.2 Routing Structure

#### Dynamic Routes (REQUIRED)
- **Tool pages**: `app/tools/[category]/[tool-id]/page.tsx`
- **Category pages**: `app/tools/[category]/page.tsx`
- **Rule**: NEVER create static route files for individual tools
- **Rule**: Use dynamic routes with `generateStaticParams()` for SSG

#### Component Loading
- **File**: `lib/tools/components.ts`
- **Rule**: Use `getToolComponent(toolId)` for dynamic component loading
- **Pattern**:
  ```typescript
  import { getToolComponent } from '@/lib/tools/components'
  const ToolComponent = await getToolComponent(tool.id)
  ```

#### Category Pages
- **Path**: `/tools/[category]`
- **Purpose**: Display all tools in a category
- **SEO**: Supports category-level keywords and aggregation
- **Note**: `/category/[category]` pages also exist (legacy), both can coexist

---

## 7. Environment Variables Standards

### 7.1 Naming Convention

#### Client-Side Variables
- **Prefix**: `NEXT_PUBLIC_`
- **Example**: `NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID`
- **Rule**: Only for variables needed in browser

#### Server-Side Variables
- **No prefix**: No `NEXT_PUBLIC_`
- **Example**: `SUPABASE_URL`, `DB_PASSWORD`
- **Rule**: For server-only variables (security)

#### Critical Variables
- `SUPABASE_URL` - Server-side only
- `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` - Server-side only
- `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASSWORD` - Server-side only

---

## 8. Component Structure Standards

### 8.1 Tool Component Structure

#### Standard Structure
```tsx
'use client'

import { useState, useEffect } from 'react'
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button'
import Input from '@/components/ui/Input'
import { trackUsage } from '@/lib/tracking'
import UsageInstructions from '@/components/shared/UsageInstructions'

export default function ToolName() {
  // 1. State declarations
  const [state, setState] = useState(...)
  
  // 2. Effects (if needed)
  useEffect(() => { ... }, [])
  
  // 3. Event handlers
  const handleAction = () => { ... }
  
  // 4. Render
  return (
    <div className="space-y-6">
      {/* Input/Controls */}
      {/* Display/Output */}
      <UsageInstructions items={[...]} />
    </div>
  )
}
```

#### Required Elements
- ✅ Usage instructions using `UsageInstructions` component
- ✅ Proper error handling
- ✅ Dark mode support
- ✅ Responsive design
- ✅ Usage tracking (on actual use, not on mount)

