## 11. File Organization Standards

### 11.1 Directory Structure

```
components/
  shared/          # Shared components (reusable across tools)
  tools/           # Tool-specific components (organized by category)
    random/        # Random category tools
    time/          # Time category tools
    text/          # Text category tools
    utilities/     # Utilities category tools
  ui/              # Base UI components (Button, Input, etc.)

lib/
  tools/
    components.ts  # Tool component mapping and loader
    data/          # Tool data (can be split by category if needed)
  *.ts             # Utility functions, shared logic

hooks/
  *.ts             # Custom React hooks (create if needed)

app/
  tools/
    [category]/           # Dynamic category route
      page.tsx             # Category page
      [tool-id]/
        page.tsx           # Tool page (dynamic route)
  category/        # Legacy category pages (can coexist)
```

### 11.2 Tool Component Organization (CRITICAL)

**CRITICAL: All tool components MUST be organized by category.**

#### Required Structure
```
components/tools/
  ├── random/          # Random category (7 tools)
  │   ├── DrawLots.tsx
  │   ├── RandomNumber.tsx
  │   ├── FlipCoin.tsx
  │   ├── RollDice.tsx
  │   ├── Roulette.tsx
  │   ├── RandomTeam.tsx
  │   └── RandomList.tsx
  ├── time/            # Time category (5 tools)
  │   ├── DigitalClock.tsx
  │   ├── CountdownTimer.tsx
  │   ├── Stopwatch.tsx
  │   ├── PomodoroTimer.tsx
  │   └── AnalogClock.tsx
  ├── text/            # Text category (3 tools)
  │   ├── FontGenerator.tsx
  │   ├── InstagramFonts.tsx
  │   └── TextToSpeech.tsx
  └── utilities/       # Utilities category (5 tools)
      ├── Counter.tsx
      ├── Scoreboard.tsx
      ├── Symbol.tsx
      ├── EmojiList.tsx
      └── PercentageCalculator.tsx
```

#### Rules
- ✅ **MUST organize by category**: Each tool component in its category folder
- ✅ **Category folders**: `random/`, `time/`, `text/`, `utilities/`
- ✅ **Component mapping**: Register in `lib/tools/components.ts`
- ❌ **NEVER place tools directly in `components/tools/`** (flat structure)
- ❌ **NEVER create static route files** for individual tools

#### Component Registration
- **File**: `lib/tools/components.ts`
- **Rule**: All tool components MUST be registered in `toolComponentMap`
- **Pattern**:
  ```typescript
  export const toolComponentMap: Record<string, () => Promise<{ default: ComponentType<any> }>> = {
    'random-number': () => import('@/components/tools/random/RandomNumber'),
    'flip-coin': () => import('@/components/tools/random/FlipCoin'),
    // ...
  }
  ```

#### Benefits
- ✅ Clear logical grouping by functionality
- ✅ Easy to locate specific tools
- ✅ Supports code splitting by category
- ✅ Scalable to 100-200+ tools
- ✅ Better IDE performance (fewer files per folder)

### 11.3 Naming Conventions

#### Components
- ✅ PascalCase: `FontGenerator.tsx`, `UsageInstructions.tsx`
- ✅ Descriptive names: `HistoryDisplay.tsx` not `History.tsx`
- ✅ Location: `components/tools/[category]/ComponentName.tsx`

#### Utilities
- ✅ camelCase: `clipboard-utils.ts`, `time-utils.ts`
- ✅ Descriptive names with purpose: `font-utils.ts`

#### Hooks
- ✅ camelCase with `use` prefix: `useLocalStorage.ts`, `useTimer.ts`

#### Tool IDs
- ✅ Use kebab-case: `random-number`, `flip-coin`, `countdown-timer`
- ✅ Descriptive and SEO-friendly
- ✅ Match component file names (without extension)

