## 15. Git & Version Control Standards

### 15.1 Commit Message Rules

- ✅ Use clear, descriptive commit messages
- ✅ Reference issue numbers if applicable
- ✅ Use English for commit messages

---

## 16. Refactoring Guidelines

### 16.1 When to Refactor

Refactor when:
- ✅ Same pattern appears in 2+ components
- ✅ Code duplication > 10 lines
- ✅ Component becomes hard to maintain
- ✅ Performance issues identified

### 16.2 Refactoring Process

1. Identify duplicate patterns
2. Create shared component/utility
3. Update all affected components
4. Test thoroughly
5. Update documentation

---

## 17. Project-Specific Rules

### 17.1 Tool Usage Tracking

- ✅ Track usage on actual user interaction (not on mount)
- ✅ Use `trackUsage(toolId)` from `@/lib/tracking`
- ✅ Only track once per session (use `hasTracked` state)

### 17.2 LocalStorage Usage

- ✅ Use `saveToStorage()` and `getFromStorage()` from `@/lib/utils`
- ✅ Provide meaningful storage keys
- ✅ Handle storage errors gracefully

### 17.3 Theme Provider

- ✅ Wrap app with `ThemeProvider` from `@/components/shared/ThemeProvider`
- ✅ Use `useTheme()` hook for theme access
- ✅ Never access `localStorage` directly for theme

